    "text": "Let πe (G) denote the set of orders of elements of a group G. A group G is\nsaid to be an OCn -group if πe (G) = {1, 2, . . . , n}. Is every OCn -group locally finite?\nDo there exist infinite OCn -groups for n ⩾ 7?                                   W. J. Shi",
